  "verdict_15_2d": "Correction restores readout-unbiasedness on both routes (single-copy residual ~0.01 at n<=4, with a residual at n>=5 from the readout ASYMMETRY, the 1/(1-p10-p01) rescaling being exact only for symmetric readout, plus finite-sample noise from the inflated variance; collective residual = channel bias only). Variance cost: single-copy 1.4x->26x (n=2->6, M=2000); collective 2.6x->12x. The single-copy correction is the steeper cost, which is why S3 still moves n* smaller."
 },
